

{% doc %}
  Filled color dot, centered in its own bordered, square cell (a faint
  left rule completes the square against the wares_spotlight box's own
  top/right/bottom borders). The cell is a square (aspect-ratio: 1,
  matched to the row's own stretched height) flush against the box's
  top/right/bottom edges: margin-block cancels the row's own vertical
  padding, margin-right cancels the row's padding-inline-end, so the
  divider line lands exactly one cell-width in from the box's right
  border and the region it encloses is a true square, not just tall.
  The dot is sized as a percentage of the cell via width/height (not
  padding) because percentage padding resolves against the *containing
  block's* width, not the cell's own -- on a narrow cell that silently
  collapsed the dot to 0x0. A plain <span class="..."> can't be entered
  through a richtext "text" setting (Shopify's sanitizer strips
  class/style attributes there), so this renders as raw block markup
  instead.
{% enddoc %}

<span class="wares-swatch-cell" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
  <span class="wares-swatch-dot"></span>
</span>

{% stylesheet %}
  .wares-swatch-cell {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    align-self: stretch;
    aspect-ratio: 1;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    margin-block: -16px;
    margin-right: -20px;
    border-left: 1px solid #C24F2E;
  }

  .wares-swatch-dot {
    display: inline-block;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    width: 82%;
    height: 82%;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: #C24F2E;
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Swatch dot",
  "tag": null
}
{% endschema %}
